{"r":2,"c":[[57,"8.3 Power Supply Recommendations"]]}
{"r":3,"c":[[57,"The input circuitry of the device can accurately measure signals on common-mode voltages beyond the power"]]}
{"r":4,"c":[[57,"supply voltage, V"],[144,". For example, the voltage applied to the V"],[348,"power supply terminal can be 5V, whereas the"]]}
{"r":5,"c":[[134,"VS"],[335,"VS"]]}
{"r":6,"c":[[57,"load power-supply voltage being monitored (the common-mode voltage) can be as high as 36V. Note also that"]]}
{"r":7,"c":[[57,"the device can withstand the full 0V to 36V range at the input terminals, regardless of whether the device has"]]}
{"r":8,"c":[[57,"power applied or not."]]}
{"r":9,"c":[[57,"Place the required power-supply bypass capacitors as close as possible to the supply and ground terminals of"]]}
{"r":10,"c":[[57,"the device to provide stability. A typical value for this supply bypass capacitor is 0.1μF. Applications with noisy or"]]}
{"r":11,"c":[[57,"high-impedance power supplies can require additional decoupling capacitors to reject power-supply noise."]]}
